<mujocoinclude>
  <!--
    flange_payload.xml  —  Calibrated tool-payload fragment for the TOOL model.

    Intended to be AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/calibrate_payload_gravity.py:
      set payload_calibration.fragment_out -> franka_emika_panda/flange_payload.xml
      set payload_calibration.body_name    -> flange_payload
    then re-run the calibration. DO NOT EDIT BY HAND once a real tool calibration
    exists; re-run the script to regenerate.

    Lumped tool payload (mass + CoM) in the ft_sensor_site frame. <include>d by
    panda_impedance_tool.xml inside <body name="ft_frame"> after the site, so this
    body frame IS the ft_sensor_site frame and the CoM drops straight into pos.
    The FT sensor measures only the tool BELOW it — the FT-sensor body itself is
    modelled separately and must NOT be added here. Rotational inertia is not
    measured by the gravity fit (irrelevant to RNE); diaginertia is carried over.

    PLACEHOLDER VALUES: seeded from ft_payload.xml (hand+stick assembly, fit
    2026-06-08) pending a dedicated calibration of the actual tool+stick payload.
    Re-run scripts/calibrate_payload_gravity.py to replace these with the measured
    tool mass/CoM.
  -->
  <body name="flange_payload" pos="0 0 0">
    <inertial mass="0.854243" pos="0.004321 -0.003973 0.040417"
              diaginertia="0.0011 0.00275 0.00187"/>
  </body>
</mujocoinclude>
